# Local .terraform directories
.terraform/

# .tfstate files
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Crash log files
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Exclude all .tfvars files, which are likely to contain sensitive data, such as
# password, private keys, and other secrets. These should not be part of version
# control as they are data points which are potentially sensitive and subject
# to change depending on the environment.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# Ignore override files as they are usually used to override resources locally and so
# are not checked in
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Ignore transient lock info files created by terraform apply
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Include override files you do wish to add to version control using negated pattern
# !example_override.tf

# Include tfplan files to ignore the plan output of command: terraform plan -out=tfplan
# example: *tfplan*

# Ignore CLI configuration files
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# Ansible vault password
.ansible_vault_pass
.aider*

# Compiled binaries: nothing executable belongs in git. A 57 MB `kubectl` was
# tracked under ansible/k3s-cluster/ (a vendored upstream copy), making the repo
# ~80x larger and putting a third-party build in a public repo's supply chain.
ansible/k3s-cluster/kubectl

# Agent session notes: local-only by design. It was tracked and therefore public
# for the repo's life (see ADR-048). Its engineering standards moved to CLAUDE.md
# and its hardware detail to docs/HARDWARE.md; nothing tracked is lost.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Internal operational trackers (2026-07-09): this repo is also a public
# portfolio artifact (see ADR-048). AUDIT.md/AUTONOMY-STATUS.md/
# IAC-GAPS.md are working incident/audit logs -- REL-0xx findings, live
# credential rotation narratives, internal investigation detail -- useful
# for day-to-day ops but not portfolio material and not something that
# should accumulate indefinitely in a public repo's history going forward.
# Content preserved outside this repo (not deleted), tracking stopped here
# rather than rewriting existing git history -- matches this repo's
# established norm of not rewriting history without a specific reason to.
docs/AUDIT.md
docs/AUTONOMY-STATUS.md
docs/IAC-GAPS.md
docs/STATUS.md
docs/secrets-inventory.md
docs/runbooks/pending-major-upgrades.md
.kube/
